  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "",
    "plain": "The classical Borsuk-Ulam theorem says that any continuous map from Sⁿ to Rⁿ must send some pair of antipodal points to the same value. This generalizes to equivariant maps under group actions: for a group G acting on spheres S(V) and S(W), there is a minimum \"Borsuk-Ulam dimension\" below which no equivariant map can avoid coincidences.",
